<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Entities, enums, constants, the appointment state machine and domain exceptions.

    One package reference, and only one. Microsoft.Extensions.Identity.Stores carries the
    IdentityUser<TKey> and IdentityRole<TKey> base types that ApplicationUser and
    ApplicationRole extend. It is the Identity *model*, not the web stack: it brings no
    EF Core, no DbContext, no ASP.NET Core hosting.

    The alternative would be to move ApplicationUser out of Domain, but every entity here
    has a navigation to it - a vehicle has an owner, an appointment has a customer, a
    review has an author - so the person is unavoidably a domain concept. Pushing it into
    Infrastructure would invert the dependency and force Domain to reference Infrastructure.

    The rule this project actually holds to is that Domain knows nothing about persistence:
    no EF attributes, no DbContext, no connection strings. That rule is intact.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Identity.Stores" Version="9.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
